{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01686",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.75,
      "end_seconds": 4.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.58,
      "text": "Hello, good to see you. Please sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.4,
      "end_seconds": 8.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Hello, thanks for fitting me in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 9.89,
      "end_seconds": 15.6,
      "duration_seconds": 5.71,
      "text": "Right, hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.47,
      "end_seconds": 20.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "What would you like to start with today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 21.49,
      "end_seconds": 35.21,
      "duration_seconds": 13.72,
      "text": "Sorry, you know, what was I saying, it's been feeling tired after the birth, doctor. She didn't want to come, but I insisted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 36.42,
      "end_seconds": 48.09,
      "duration_seconds": 11.67,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Pulse is 68 beats a minute, blood pressure 118 over 82, respiratory rate 14, temperature 36.6, saturation 97 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.84,
      "end_seconds": 52.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.04,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.74,
      "end_seconds": 69.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.69,
      "end_seconds": 80.78,
      "duration_seconds": 10.09,
      "text": "I've had it for two months. I didn't want to bother you but it keeps coming back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.76,
      "end_seconds": 85.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "Rate it for me, mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.11,
      "end_seconds": 93.4,
      "duration_seconds": 6.29,
      "text": "Oh, you know, a three out of ten, I suppose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.25,
      "end_seconds": 101.69,
      "duration_seconds": 7.44,
      "text": "And, And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 101.79,
      "end_seconds": 108.74,
      "duration_seconds": 6.95,
      "text": "Ah, um, tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.35,
      "end_seconds": 113.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "I, I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.27,
      "end_seconds": 120.44,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "What about bleeding that is tailing off, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.36,
      "end_seconds": 124.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Hmm, yeah. Six months, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.1,
      "end_seconds": 132.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Have you had some soreness from the stitches?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.34,
      "end_seconds": 139.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Yes, uh, actually."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.49,
      "end_seconds": 147.05,
      "duration_seconds": 5.56,
      "text": "Any fever, leg swelling or thoughts of harming the baby at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.08,
      "end_seconds": 167.21,
      "duration_seconds": 16.13,
      "text": "Erm, no, no fever, no leg swelling, no thoughts of harming the baby. I was feeling tearful at times at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.16,
      "end_seconds": 173.0,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "Have you noticed any weakness, or anything odd with your balance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.2,
      "end_seconds": 179.53,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, no, that's all normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.81,
      "end_seconds": 184.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.85,
      "end_seconds": 190.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "Glibenclamide. I take it 5 milligrams, before breakfast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 191.74,
      "end_seconds": 199.34,
      "duration_seconds": 7.6,
      "text": "She is supposed to take it before breakfast, but I can't say she always does."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.65,
      "end_seconds": 209.32,
      "duration_seconds": 8.67,
      "text": "Omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day for the reflux. Paracetamol. I take it 1 gram, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.88,
      "end_seconds": 212.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "What operations have you had, if any?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.54,
      "end_seconds": 222.23,
      "duration_seconds": 7.69,
      "text": "Right, yes, I had a caesarean for my second baby, nine years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.48,
      "end_seconds": 228.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 230.08,
      "end_seconds": 243.13,
      "duration_seconds": 13.05,
      "text": "I, I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, you know, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.44,
      "end_seconds": 247.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.8,
      "end_seconds": 263.77,
      "duration_seconds": 11.97,
      "text": "Well, I've had diabetes, yes. My neighbour said I should get it looked at. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.37,
      "end_seconds": 266.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Okay, go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.98,
      "end_seconds": 276.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "Arthritis in my knees, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.86,
      "end_seconds": 279.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "Yes, carry on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 281.31,
      "end_seconds": 283.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "Yes, acid reflux."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.0,
      "end_seconds": 288.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Right, right. Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 290.04,
      "end_seconds": 304.16,
      "duration_seconds": 14.12,
      "text": "Nothing, I'm teetotal. I smoke roughly a pack every two days. Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit. I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.99,
      "end_seconds": 329.57,
      "duration_seconds": 9.58,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. My working impression is a normal postnatal recovery. I can't rule out the baby blues yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 330.28,
      "end_seconds": 333.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "What are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 334.58,
      "end_seconds": 351.96,
      "duration_seconds": 17.38,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a normal postnatal recovery, and we'll know more once the a blood count is back. I think a blood count makes sense here, for postnatal tiredness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 353.8,
      "end_seconds": 358.97,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "We have a slot Tuesday at 3:30 pm, if that works."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 360.04,
      "end_seconds": 361.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.16,
      "text": "That's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.5,
      "end_seconds": 376.68,
      "duration_seconds": 14.18,
      "text": "Rest when the baby sleeps and ask for help; contraception can be discussed at six weeks. One warning sign to remember: the symptoms get worse. In that case don't wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 378.54,
      "end_seconds": 381.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Ah, thank you, that's clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 382.76,
      "end_seconds": 389.75,
      "duration_seconds": 6.99,
      "text": "I'd like you back in four weeks. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 391.31,
      "end_seconds": 395.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Right, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}